0..67 Comment "// A result that follows its argument. A recursive definition whose"
68..145 Comment "// result is the type it recurses on, and which holds with that result at its"
146..222 Comment "// parameter\'s own stage — every branch returns a value no larger than the"
223..304 Comment "// argument — returns at the stage of the argument a call hands it. A recursion"
305..380 Comment "// then descends through such a call: division recurses on what subtraction"
381..454 Comment "// leaves of its dividend\'s predecessor, and a logarithm on half of it. A"
455..525 Comment "// definition with no recursion opens no stage, and its result follows"
526..599 Comment "// nothing. What refuses is in `../../pathological/data/following.gandr`."
600..602 Comment "//"
603..617 Comment "// - see: #392"
619..666 Comment "// The naturals and the numerals two and three."
